{
  "chapter": "context/memory",
  "tier": "build",
  "notes": [
    "Durable facts are not strings. A fact is a record with provenance, authority, recency and",
    "resolution, and those four fields are what let contradiction have an answer.",
    "Append-only storage is the trap: the old version does not go anywhere, so both coexist and",
    "the agent has no principled way to choose. A superseded fact never wins, however recent.",
    "Highest authority first, then most recent. Without that ordering you are asking a",
    "probabilistic component to adjudicate a data-integrity question.",
    "Expiry does not delete. A stale fact is surfaced with its age, because 'net-60 as of",
    "eighteen months ago' is useful and a confident bare 'net-60' is not.",
    "Write sparingly: when a human asserts something or a system of record changes. The model's",
    "own inferences are conclusions, and conclusions belong to a run.",
    "Nothing in a memory store should be a secret. Memories are replayed verbatim into every",
    "future context that loads them.",
    "Facts are keyed by tenant. A fact learned in one customer's context is never recalled in",
    "another's.",
    "The clock is an injected integer day counter, so ageDays is exact in both languages."
  ],
